      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sandbox): add skipSkillsSync config option to suppress skill sync",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSkills are copied into the sandbox workspace on every sandbox setup. For users who do not use skills or have already deployed them through other means, this sync is unnecessary overhead.\n\nRelated: #97638\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds skipSkillsSync as an optional boolean under agents.defaults.sandbox and agents.list[].sandbox, defaulting to false.\n\nTwo key design decisions:\n1. File copying is skipped but skill eligibility and skills snapshot (prompt text + env overrides) are preserved via resolveSandboxSkillRuntimeInputs conditional snapshot logic\n2. The command/system-prompt inspection path also preserves skills by falling back to host-side snapshot when skipSkillsSync is true (instead of returning empty)\n\n## User Impact\n\n```json5\n{ agents: { defaults: { sandbox: { skipSkillsSync: true } } } }\n```\n\nSafe-use caveat: For advanced deployments where skills are preinstalled via custom Docker image, setupCommand, or readonly workspace mounts. File copying is skipped; prompt-visible skills and env overrides are preserved from session-start snapshot.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTest coverage (40 tests, all pass):\n\n| Test | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| preserves snapshot when skipSkillsSync enabled | Returns snapshot, not undefined |\n| drops snapshot when skipSkillsSync absent | Returns undefined (unchanged) |\n| skipSkillsSync from ensureSandboxWorkspaceForSession | Returns flag in workspace info |\n| skips sync (ro) + eligibility preserved | syncSkillsToWorkspace not called, eligibility returned |\n| skips sync (rw) + eligibility preserved | syncSkillsToWorkspace not called, eligibility returned |\n| requests skill sync (existing, unchanged) | sync IS called (no regression) |\n\nHost-side snapshot fallback in command/system-prompt path: When skipSkillsSync is true, the sandbox inspection path skips container-only skill loading and falls through to resolveReusableWorkspaceSkillSnapshot for host-side prompt text.\n\n13 files, +183/-28:\nsrc/config/types.agents-shared.ts (+1)\nsrc/config/zod-schema.agent-runtime.ts (+1)\nsrc/agents/sandbox/types.ts (+2)\nsrc/agents/sandbox/config.ts (+1)\nsrc/agents/sandbox/context.ts (+15/-24)\nsrc/agents/sandbox.resolveSandboxContext.test.ts (+82)\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.ts (+10/-2)\nsrc/agents/embedded-agent-runner/sandbox-skills.test.ts (+43)\nsrc/agents/cli-runner/prepare.ts (+3)\nsrc/auto-reply/reply/commands-system-prompt.ts (+66/-2)\n\nHuman-driven development with AI assistant support. TDD: tests written before production code.",
